{
  "info": {
    "name": "CIDCO Architect Handshake & Token Flow",
    "description": "End-to-end handshake, token and data flow between an architect and the CIDCO admin.\n\n## CASE 1 \u2014 first-time setup\n1. **Admin > Officer login**\n2. **Admin > Issue handshake credentials** \u2014 saves clientId + clientSecret\n3. **Architect > Validate \u2014 success** \u2014 send credentials + your station IP/device. CIDCO whitelists them and returns BOTH tokens (saved to {{accessToken}} / {{refreshToken}}).\n4. **Architect > Send AQI data** \u2014 Bearer {{accessToken}}. Schedule this every 3 hours.\n\n## CASE 2 \u2014 access token expires\n'Send AQI data' answers **503 / ACCESS_EXPIRED**. Run **Architect > Refresh access token** \u2014 you get a new access token and keep the same refresh token. Resume sending.\n\n## CASE 3 \u2014 refresh token expires\nOnce the refresh token lapses the access token dies with it, so 'Send AQI data' answers **503 / BOTH_EXPIRED**. Re-run **Architect > Validate \u2014 success** with clientId + clientSecret to get a brand-new pair, then carry on from CASE 1 step 4.\n\n## Admin controls\n**Set token policy** changes the access/refresh validity windows; **Generate token** issues a full pair from the dashboard. Both take effect on the API immediately.\n\nAdmin requests use the officer session cookie; architect requests use only credentials/tokens, exactly as an external system would.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    {
      "key": "baseUrl",
      "value": "http://localhost:3000"
    },
    {
      "key": "adminEmail",
      "value": "officer@cidco.example"
    },
    {
      "key": "adminPassword",
      "value": "Password123"
    },
    {
      "key": "architectEmail",
      "value": "architect@example.com"
    },
    {
      "key": "clientId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "clientSecret",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "handshakeId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "token",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "tokenRequestId",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "accessToken",
      "value": ""
    },
    {
      "key": "refreshToken",
      "value": ""
    }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Admin (CIDCO officer)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Officer login",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('logged in', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const u = pm.response.json().data.user;",
                  "pm.expect(u.role).to.not.eql('ARCHITECT');"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{adminEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"{{adminPassword}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/auth/login",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "auth",
                "login"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Signs in the CIDCO officer. Sets an httpOnly session cookie that the admin requests below reuse."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Issue handshake credentials",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('issued', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const c = pm.response.json().data.credential;",
                  "const h = pm.response.json().data.handshake;",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('clientId', c.clientId);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('clientSecret', c.clientSecret);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('handshakeId', h.id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"architectEmail\": \"{{architectEmail}}\",\n  \"expiresInDays\": 30\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/admin/handshakes",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "admin",
                "handshakes"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Issues the credential JSON to hand to the architect. clientSecret is returned once."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "List handshakes",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/admin/handshakes",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "admin",
                "handshakes"
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Generate tokens (mode: both | access | refresh)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('token issued', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "const t = pm.response.json().data.token;",
                  "if (t.accessToken) { pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', t.accessToken); pm.collectionVariables.set('token', t.accessToken); }",
                  "if (t.refreshToken) pm.collectionVariables.set('refreshToken', t.refreshToken);",
                  "console.log('mode:', pm.response.json().data.mode, '| access:', !!t.accessToken, '| refresh:', !!t.refreshToken);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"clientId\": \"{{clientId}}\",\n  \"clientSecret\": \"{{clientSecret}}\",\n  \"mode\": \"both\",\n  \"expiresInDays\": 7,\n  \"refreshExpiresInDays\": 30\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/admin/handshakes/{{handshakeId}}/tokens",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "admin",
                "handshakes",
                "{{handshakeId}}",
                "tokens"
              ]
            },
            "description": "CIDCO chooses which token(s) to generate via `mode`:\n- **both** (default) \u2014 new access + refresh pair; revokes any earlier pair. Give the architect both.\n- **access** \u2014 new access token only; the current refresh token keeps working.\n- **refresh** \u2014 new refresh token only; the current access token keeps working.\n\nFields not generated come back as null. 409 if the handshake has no live pair yet (use mode 'both' first) or is not ESTABLISHED."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "List token requests",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "const rows = pm.response.json().data.tokenRequests;",
                  "const pending = rows.find(r => r.status === 'PENDING');",
                  "if (pending) pm.collectionVariables.set('tokenRequestId', pending.id);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/admin/token-requests?status=PENDING",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "admin",
                "token-requests"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "status",
                  "value": "PENDING"
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Approve token request",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('approved', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('token', pm.response.json().data.token.token);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"expiresInDays\": 7\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/admin/token-requests/{{tokenRequestId}}/approve",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "admin",
                "token-requests",
                "{{tokenRequestId}}",
                "approve"
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Communication logs",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/admin/comm-logs?handshakeId={{handshakeId}}",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "admin",
                "comm-logs"
              ],
              "query": [
                {
                  "key": "handshakeId",
                  "value": "{{handshakeId}}"
                }
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Revoke handshake",
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/admin/handshakes/{{handshakeId}}/revoke",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "admin",
                "handshakes",
                "{{handshakeId}}",
                "revoke"
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Set token policy (expiry days)",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"accessTokenTtlDays\": 7,\n  \"refreshTokenTtlDays\": 30,\n  \"enforceWhitelist\": true\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/admin/handshakes/{{handshakeId}}/policy",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "admin",
                "handshakes",
                "{{handshakeId}}",
                "policy"
              ]
            },
            "description": "CIDCO sets the access/refresh validity windows and whether the IP whitelist is enforced. Applies to every token issued afterwards."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Set expiry date on the live token pair",
          "request": {
            "method": "PATCH",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"accessExpiresAt\": \"2026-09-01T00:00:00Z\",\n  \"refreshExpiresAt\": \"2026-10-01T00:00:00Z\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/admin/handshakes/{{handshakeId}}/token-expiry",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "admin",
                "handshakes",
                "{{handshakeId}}",
                "token-expiry"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Overrides the expiry dates on the pair the architect already holds."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Reset IP/device whitelist",
          "request": {
            "method": "DELETE",
            "header": [],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/admin/handshakes/{{handshakeId}}/whitelist",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "admin",
                "handshakes",
                "{{handshakeId}}",
                "whitelist"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Clears the registered IP/device so the architect can register a new machine on the next validate."
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "name": "Architect (Postman only)",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Validate \u2014 success (200, establishes channel)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('established', () => pm.response.to.have.status(200));",
                  "const d = pm.response.json().data;",
                  "pm.expect(d.established).to.be.true;",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', d.accessToken);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('refreshToken', d.refreshToken);",
                  "pm.collectionVariables.set('token', d.accessToken);",
                  "console.log('access exp days', d.expiresInDays, '| refresh exp days', d.refreshExpiresInDays);"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"clientId\": \"{{clientId}}\",\n  \"clientSecret\": \"{{clientSecret}}\",\n  \"ipAddress\": \"{{$randomIP}}\",\n  \"deviceInfo\": \"RaspberryPi-4 | station STN-KHR-07\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/architect/validate",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "architect",
                "validate"
              ]
            },
            "description": "CASE 1. Send credentials plus the IP/device to whitelist. Returns BOTH tokens. NOTE: replace {{$randomIP}} with your real station IP \u2014 CIDCO whitelists whatever you send here and later calls must match it."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Validate \u2014 failure (expect 504)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('rejected with 504', () => pm.response.to.have.status(504));"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"clientId\": \"{{clientId}}\",\n  \"clientSecret\": \"hs_sec_wrong_secret\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/architect/validate",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "architect",
                "validate"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Demonstrates the 504 the CIDCO protocol returns when validation fails."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Send AQI data (Bearer token)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 503) {",
                  "  const d = pm.response.json().details || {};",
                  "  console.log('TOKEN EXPIRED ->', d.reason, '| action:', d.action);",
                  "  pm.test('503 carries recovery action', () => pm.expect(d.action).to.be.a('string'));",
                  "} else {",
                  "  pm.test('stored', () => pm.response.to.have.status(201));",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              },
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{accessToken}}"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"projectSiteId\": \"CIDCO-KHR-012\",\n  \"monitoringStationId\": \"STN-KHR-07\",\n  \"oem\": \"Aeroqual\",\n  \"deviceModel\": \"AQY-1\",\n  \"measuredAt\": \"{{$isoTimestamp}}\",\n  \"aqiValue\": 176,\n  \"pm25\": 78.3,\n  \"pm10\": 152.9,\n  \"no2\": 41.2,\n  \"so2\": 12.7,\n  \"co\": 0.9,\n  \"ozone\": 48.6,\n  \"temperature\": 33.4,\n  \"humidity\": 62.1,\n  \"integrationMethod\": \"Automated API (3h)\",\n  \"otherParams\": { \"windSpeed\": 3.2, \"windDir\": \"NW\", \"noise_dB\": 58 }\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/architect/data",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "architect",
                "data"
              ]
            },
            "description": "Full monitoring-station payload. `measuredAt` uses the {{$isoTimestamp}} dynamic variable, so scheduling this request (\u22ef \u2192 Schedule run, or a Monitor) every 3 hours feeds a fresh reading into CIDCO's database on each run. CIDCO stamps the Data Receipt Timestamp itself. For photos, switch the body to form-data and add 'document' and 'boardPhotos' file fields."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Refresh access token (CASE 2)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "if (pm.response.code === 200) {",
                  "  const d = pm.response.json().data;",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('accessToken', d.accessToken);",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('token', d.accessToken);",
                  "  pm.test('access token renewed', () => pm.expect(d.accessToken).to.be.a('string'));",
                  "} else if (pm.response.code === 503) {",
                  "  console.log('CASE 3 \u2014 refresh token expired. Re-run Validate with clientId + clientSecret.');",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Content-Type",
                "value": "application/json"
              }
            ],
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"refreshToken\": \"{{refreshToken}}\"\n}"
            },
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/architect/refresh",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "architect",
                "refresh"
              ]
            },
            "description": "CASE 2 \u2014 run this when 'Send AQI data' returns 503 / ACCESS_EXPIRED. Returns a new access token; your refresh token stays the same. If this itself returns 503 / BOTH_EXPIRED that is CASE 3: re-run 'Validate \u2014 success'."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Status",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "x-client-id",
                "value": "{{clientId}}"
              },
              {
                "key": "x-client-secret",
                "value": "{{clientSecret}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/architect/status",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "architect",
                "status"
              ]
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Logs (timestamped)",
          "request": {
            "method": "GET",
            "header": [
              {
                "key": "Authorization",
                "value": "Bearer {{token}}"
              }
            ],
            "url": {
              "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/api/architect/logs",
              "host": [
                "{{baseUrl}}"
              ],
              "path": [
                "api",
                "architect",
                "logs"
              ]
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}